From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: quiet flow re-arms while the table is full

A flow whose hardware entry saw no hits across two refreshes is re-armed
(dropped and programmed afresh), with one ratelimited line. That line
printed the TC cookie, which is the flowtable's tuple pointer: a raw
kernel address in a log that is often forwarded off the box.

While the flow table is full the line is also constant noise. Many
connections then have only one direction in hardware; the other is
refused, crosses the software path and refreshes the flow about once a
second, and the hardware direction is re-armed whenever it saw no
packet in between. On a GL-BE9300 filled with 2000 NATed UDP flows
that was about 8000 re-arms a minute at 3.6% CPU in total. The re-arms
are harmless (the CPU-path packet rate matched what was refused, so
the hardware halves kept forwarding), but the log was flooded.

Print the flow's table index instead of the cookie, and while a
full-table episode (see the previous patch) is running, report re-arms
at debug level only. A re-arm outside an episode, the case the re-arm
was added for, still gets its ratelimited line.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c
@@ -864,6 +864,15 @@ static void ppe_offload_flow_disown(stru
  */
 #define PPE_OFFLOAD_FLOW_FULL_QUIET	(60 * HZ)
 
+/* Whether a refused add was seen within the last PPE_OFFLOAD_FLOW_FULL_QUIET,
+ * i.e. a full-table episode is still running. Under priv->lock.
+ */
+static bool ppe_offload_flow_tbl_full_recent(const struct ppe_offload_priv *priv)
+{
+	return priv->flow_full_last &&
+	       time_before(jiffies, priv->flow_full_last + PPE_OFFLOAD_FLOW_FULL_QUIET);
+}
+
 /* Hardware refuses a hash-mode add (-ENOSPC) when every way of the key's
  * bucket is taken. Report it with the table's occupancy, counted from the
  * driver's own slot bookkeeping, so a full table can be told apart from a
@@ -871,8 +880,7 @@ static void ppe_offload_flow_disown(stru
  */
 static void ppe_offload_flow_tbl_full(struct ppe_offload_priv *priv)
 {
-	bool new_episode = !priv->flow_full_last ||
-			   time_after(jiffies, priv->flow_full_last + PPE_OFFLOAD_FLOW_FULL_QUIET);
+	bool new_episode = !ppe_offload_flow_tbl_full_recent(priv);
 	unsigned int i, used = 0;
 
 	priv->flow_full_last = jiffies ?: 1;
@@ -1470,8 +1478,18 @@ static int ppe_offload_flow_replace(stru
 			stage = "exists";
 			goto unlock;
 		}
-		pr_info_ratelimited("ppe_offload: flow %lx re-armed: hardware entry idle across refreshes\n",
-				    cls->cookie);
+		/* While the table is full, many connections have only one
+		 * direction in hardware; the other crosses the software path
+		 * and refreshes the flow, and a direction that saw no packet
+		 * in between is re-armed here as a matter of course. Only a
+		 * re-arm outside such an episode is worth a line.
+		 */
+		if (ppe_offload_flow_tbl_full_recent(priv))
+			pr_debug("ppe_offload: flow entry %u re-armed while the table is full\n",
+				 entry->flow_index);
+		else
+			pr_info_ratelimited("ppe_offload: flow entry %u re-armed: no hardware hits across refreshes\n",
+					    entry->flow_index);
 		ppe_offload_flow_forget(priv, entry);
 	}
 
